 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Totally normal. Lots of people never get over it. How far is it? Ten miles or fifty? Short commutes can often find slower routes through parks that never have traffic. If it's decent length, an easy train line might make it fast compared to driving. A bus with a station stop every mile gives good confidence too. If you pick a park route, look for signs of life before you approach. People often leave parks just as you' arriving, so start a little early.",
